# farfield os — sway config for the rack touch-panel kiosk.
#
# Replaces mango: sway exposes wl_touch, so foot turns a tap into a click and
# ff-board's on-screen buttons + tap-to-fullscreen work; it also hides the
# cursor for touch. Launched by ~/.zprofile on tty1 when a display is
# attached. The six dashboard panels are tiled into a 3x2 grid by
# ff-kiosk-tiles (sway has no auto-grid layout).

### appearance — farfield (docs/BRAND.md): Deep Space field, hairline
### borders, Horizon orange only on the focused tile — the signal. A thin
### 2px border + gaps is the only chrome (the board renders its panels
### borderless, edge-to-edge).
output * bg #0e222d solid_color
default_orientation horizontal
default_border pixel 2
default_floating_border pixel 2
font pango:monospace 8
gaps inner 6
gaps outer 8
smart_gaps off
#                        border  bg      text    indicator child_border
client.focused          #e59f67 #0e222d #f3e5d1 #e59f67 #e59f67
client.focused_inactive #2e3d44 #0e222d #6a8699 #2e3d44 #2e3d44
client.unfocused        #2e3d44 #0e222d #6a8699 #2e3d44 #2e3d44

### input — hide the cursor shortly after it stops moving (touch panel).
seat * hide_cursor 1500

### dashboard tiles
for_window [app_id="ff-.*"] border pixel 2
exec ff-kiosk-tiles

### walk-up keybindings (only matter with a keyboard plugged in)
bindsym Mod4+f fullscreen toggle
bindsym Mod4+Shift+r reload
bindsym Mod4+Shift+q exit
